    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the turnover rate thing is interesting. how would u factor in things like the \"character\" of a neighborhood? like, when we see high turnover or more transient populations, it usually correlates with higher risk in our initial tests. would u suggest weighting specific zip codes or even the types of local amenities (like certain types of retail vs more established services) to help the model distinguish between \"stable\" and \"unstable\" areas?",
