      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can certainly use zip codes as categorical features, but consider incorporating granular socioeconomic data like median income stratification rather than just the zip code itself. Differentiating neighborhood \"character\" is achievable by weighting features based on the mix of local amenities; for instance, a higher density of established services versus fast-turnover retail might suggest greater stability. This approach allows your model to learn the nuances between different types of transient or stable environments.",
